      "description": "Consume one owned branch as support and one owned viable woody-cutting as propagation material on an unoccupied forest cell. Create a persistent shared woody nursery. First branch after 24 rounds, then at most one branch every 12 rounds, ground-stock ceiling 2 and lifetime production 6. Anyone can collect mature ground branches with pickup. Production records environmental biomass units; branch nutritional energy is zero. No tending, immediate output, natural-site refill or occupied-cell/lifetime reset. The registered collect-woody-cutting mechanic extracts one cutting from adjacent finite matching tree stock, but personal learning is required separately.",
